/**
 * An undici Agent whose DNS resolution is hard-wired to an already-vetted
 * address. Host and SNI still come from the URL, so virtual hosts and TLS
 * certificate validation behave normally — only the address we dial is fixed.
 *
 * undici's connector calls `lookup` with `{ all: true }` and expects an ARRAY of
 * `{ address, family }`; node's plain `net.connect` contract is the positional
 * `(err, address, family)` form. Getting this wrong does not throw at build
 * time, it just fails every request at runtime ("Invalid IP address: undefined"),
 * so both shapes are answered here.
